# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GUARD RAILS. These block the files that still contain participants' real
# names. Do not remove them.
#
# Git history is permanent: if any of these is committed even once, deleting it
# in a later commit does NOT remove it from the repository, and on a public
# repo it may already have been cloned, forked or indexed.
#
# NOTE: do not add a bare "Data/" or "Output/" rule here. Git on Windows sets
# core.ignorecase=true, so those also match this repository's own pseudonymised
# "data/" directory and would silently exclude the entire dataset from commits.
# The raw collection tree lives outside this repository; the patterns below
# catch it by its distinctive contents instead of by directory name.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The participant_id -> real name mapping. This is the re-identification key.
participants.csv
**/participants.csv

# Raw collection tree, if ever copied in: its per-session directory names embed
# participants' real names, e.g. "33004-42675 - FIRSTNAME SURNAME - 22 Nov 2020".
Week [0-9]/
Week [0-9][0-9]/
**/Week [0-9]/
*timings.txt
*accuracy.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large regenerable outputs (~1.5 GB), well over GitHub's limits
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.parquet
*.pkl
results/
**/results/
Result/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Exception: paper 2's summary tables are small and are part of the release.
# The directory has to be un-excluded first, because git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded. Everything inside is then excluded
# again and only .csv and .txt are allowed back, so caches, Parquet trial files
# and model weights stay out even if they are written here by a run.
!paper2/results/
paper2/results/*
!paper2/results/*.csv
!paper2/results/*.txt

# LaTeX build artefacts
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz
